# Commits that changed formatting or comments only, never behaviour.
#
# `git blame` skips these, so a line is attributed to the commit that last changed what the code
# DOES rather than to a sweep that reflowed the prose around it. GitHub honours this file
# automatically; locally, turn it on once per clone:
#
#     git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# Add a commit here only if it is provably behaviour-neutral — for a change under the scanner, that
# means the scan output over a fixed corpus is byte-identical before and after.
#
# Format: one full 40-character SHA per line, newest last, with the subject as a comment above it.

